  "claim": "The Minardi M189 was a race series car that was replaced by a newer model. Pirelli, a Milan based company, made the tires for the newer version. Frank Gardner was a racing driver who drove in the racing series.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Minardi M190. Sentence: The car was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and ran on Pirelli tyres.\nPage: Pirelli. Sentence: Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company based in Milan, Italy, formerly listed on the Milan Stock Exchange since 1922, but now an overseas subsidiary of Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\nPage: Minardi M189. Sentence: Updated as the M189B for the season, it was used for the first two races of the year before being replaced by the Minardi M190.\nPage: Frank Gardner (racing driver). Sentence: He was European F5000 champion, and participated in nine World Championship Formula One Grands Prix, debuting on 11 July 1964.",
