        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina\n- People: Frank Gardner\n- Topics: Formula One, European F5000 Championship\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Gardner debuted in the World Championship Formula One on 11 July 1964.\n- Frank Gardner participated in nine World Championship Formula One Grands Prix.\n- Frank Gardner was a European F5000 champion.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. has been based in Milan, Italy, and was formerly listed on the Milan Stock Exchange since 1922.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company and is now an overseas subsidiary of the Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\n- The Minardi M189 was updated as the M189B for the season.\n- The Minardi M189B was used for the first two races of the year before being replaced by the Minardi M190.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and ran on Pirelli tyres.",
